  "$doc": "Recolour schemes for imported pack models (docs/art-style.md section 3). Every texel of a model's palette texture is sorted into a colour family by hue (neutral = low saturation) and replaced by the scheme's ramp for that family, picked by the texel's lightness (dark -> light). Texels of a family listed in 'glow' become emissive only when they are bright and saturated (eyes, runes, corruption), so large dark areas never glow. A model in data/models.json picks a scheme with 'palette'; content variants can use any scheme. blight_scrap: Blight war machines (dark slate hull, crimson plates). blight_pale: lighter Blight hides for models that read as black blobs at distance.",
